---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import '../styles/projects.css';
const user = Astro.locals.user;
---

<Base
  title="Sample client review report"
  description="See how a before-and-after website report explains a change and gives clients clear next steps."
>
  <SiteHeader user={user} />
  <main class="report-page">
    <p class="notice">
      Illustrative example · Fictional client and page layouts. These are not captured websites or measured results.
    </p>
    <header>
      <span class="eyebrow">NORTH STUDIO · CLIENT WEBSITE REVIEW</span>
      <h1>A clearer path to booking.</h1>
      <p>Example client: Fieldwork Studio · Desktop homepage review</p>
    </header>
    <section>
      <h2>What changed</h2>
      <p>
        The revised page puts the service and booking action first. The review notes explain what to check before
        approving the update.
      </p>
    </section>
    <div class="review-images">
      <figure>
        <h2>Before · baseline</h2>
        <p class="report-meta">
          Illustrative desktop layout · example.com · 1440 × 900 CSS px
          <br />
          Example baseline: 10 September 2026, 09:00 UTC
        </p>
        <div
          class="sample-frame before"
          role="img"
          aria-label="Fictional baseline homepage with a vague headline and a low-contrast contact button"
        >
          <div class="sample-nav">
            FIELDWORK <small>About · Work · Contact</small>
          </div>
          <div class="sample-body">
            <span>WELCOME TO OUR WEBSITE</span>
            <h3>
              Ideas for
              <br />
              what comes next.
            </h3>
            <p>We bring creativity and experience to every project.</p>
            <span class="sample-button">Learn more</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <h2>After · ready for review</h2>
        <p class="report-meta">
          Illustrative desktop layout · example.com · 1440 × 900 CSS px
          <br />
          Example update: 11 September 2026, 14:00 UTC
        </p>
        <div
          class="sample-frame after"
          role="img"
          aria-label="Fictional updated homepage with a specific service headline and a prominent booking button"
        >
          <div class="sample-nav">
            FIELDWORK <small>Services · Work · Book a call</small>
          </div>
          <div class="sample-body">
            <span>WEB DESIGN FOR SMALL BUSINESSES</span>
            <h3>
              Your next client
              <br />
              starts here.
            </h3>
            <p>A clear website. A simple way to get in touch.</p>
            <span class="sample-button">Book a discovery call ↗</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <section class="project-panel" style="margin-top:24px">
      <h2>Review notes</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>The headline now names the service and audience.</li>
        <li>The booking action is visible in the first screen.</li>
        <li>Before approval, test the booking form and check the mobile layout.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        <strong>Review status: Needs review.</strong> Screenshots document appearance; they do not prove the form works
        or that conversion improved.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="project-panel" style="margin-top:24px">
      <h2>Make this workflow yours</h2>
      <p>
        Create a project, capture a baseline and an updated page, then add your notes. Share a web report with an
        expiring link or export a branded PDF on a paid plan.
      </p>
      <div class="project-links">
        <a class="btn btn--ink" href={user ? '/app/start' : '/signup?next=%2Fapp%2Fstart'}>
          Create your first report
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn--outline" href="/pricing">
          Compare plans
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="small muted">
        This example uses no screenshot quota. Real reports keep their source images’ original retention period.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Base>
<style>
  .sample-frame {
    border: 1px solid var(--line-2);
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
    min-height: 350px;
  }
  .sample-nav {
    padding: 20px;
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 800;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 12px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
  }
  .sample-nav small {
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .sample-body {
    padding: 32px 24px;
  }
  .sample-body > span:first-child {
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }
  .sample-body h3 {
    font-size: clamp(26px, 3vw, 38px);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin: 20px 0;
  }
  .sample-body p {
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .sample-button {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 12px 15px;
    font-size: 12px;
    border-radius: 7px;
  }
  .before {
    background: #eeeae2;
    color: #615e56;
  }
  .before .sample-button {
    border: 1px solid #8d887c;
  }
  .after {
    background: #20251e;
    color: #fff;
  }
  .after .sample-nav {
    border-color: #465041;
  }
  .after .sample-button {
    background: #d6ed8c;
    color: #20251e;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
</style>
